  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math> be an integer. If the shortest distance between the lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>z</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math> then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>&#955;</mi></mfenced></math> is _______."
  },
